// `serve`: the site in `public/`, GitHub login, publish tokens, trusted
// publishing and the publish / yank API over plain HTTP (TLS ends at a
// reverse proxy).
//
// One thread per connection. A write to the data (registry.sqlite3,
// tables.nabi) reads it and writes it back under `LOCK`, in one
// transaction; an index commit and push holds `INDEX` (taken before
// `LOCK`, never inside it). Neither is held across a fetch of a package
// source or a call to GitHub. Reads take no lock: each reads a snapshot
// of the database. After an index commit `STALE` is set and a background
// thread rebuilds the site by running this program again.
//
// Here: the settings, the responses every route builds, the connection
// loop and the rebuild. `routes` picks the answer to a request; `api`,
// `auth`, `account`, `owners` and `admin` are the routes behind it;
// `store` is the data, kept in SQLite by `tables` through `sqlite`;
// `github` the calls to GitHub, `limit` the rate limits, `names` which
// new names are taken, and `mail` the notices sent through Amazon SES
// (`aws`) by a thread of their own.

pub mod account;
pub mod admin;
pub mod advisories;
pub mod api;
pub mod auth;
pub mod aws;
pub mod delete;
pub mod downloads;
pub mod github;
pub mod img;
pub mod limit;
pub mod mail;
pub mod names;
pub mod owners;
pub mod routes;
pub mod sqlite;
pub mod store;
pub mod tables;

